<title>JAPAN: BOJ refrains from money market operation--traders.</title>
<headline>BOJ refrains from money market operation--traders.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Japan (BOJ) refrained from its regular 9.20 a.m. (0020 GMT) money market operation on Monday, money traders said.</p>
<p>The money market had a surplus of about 190 billion yen going into the day.</p>
